WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.818
Nodes can feed each other, and they can feed back.

2
00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:07.062
Start with Noise: a new random value on every frame.

3
00:00:07.518 --> 00:00:08.860
Raw noise is jittery.

4
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.951
A resonant low-pass filter turns it into a slow, rubbery wobble.

5
00:00:15.532 --> 00:00:18.991
Send the filtered noise to H Position, Rotation and Z Push.

6
00:00:18.991 --> 00:00:21.337
The raster drifts like it is underwater.

7
00:00:21.791 --> 00:00:25.887
Param Out reads any parameter's live value back into the graph.

8
00:00:25.887 --> 00:00:27.317
This one reads Z Push.

9
00:00:27.773 --> 00:00:30.838
Delay it by thirty frames, half a second, and scale it up.

10
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:45.030
Now close the loop: send the delayed copy back into Z Push.

11
00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.846
The depth chases its own echo.

12
00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.631
Keep the loop gain below one, or it runs away.

13
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:50.958
Probe the loop.

14
00:00:50.958 --> 00:00:52.874
No two cycles are quite the same.

15
00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.610
Restore the window, and let it run.

16
00:00:59.947 --> 00:01:02.519
Feedback is where the strange stuff lives.

17
00:01:02.519 --> 00:01:04.602
Keep the amounts small, and nudge.

18
00:01:04.602 --> 00:01:07.052
Next: the camera as a modulation source.
